{{also|Drucken|drücken|Drücken}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*þrukjaną||to press}}, {{m|gem-pro|*þrūganą||to threaten}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*trūk-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*trūg-||to press, beat}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|drukken||to press, print}}, {{cog|da|trykke||to press}}, {{cog|en|thrutch||to throng}} and, outside Germanic, with {{cog|sq|ndryqem||to stretch}}. Closely cognate with {{cog|de|drücken||to press, push}}: ''drucken'' is originally the southern form; the first German printers were in the south.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈdʁʊkŋ̩]|[ˈdʁʊkən]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-drucken.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-drucken.ogg|Audio (Austria)|lang=de}}

